      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "We start with the equation given in the problem:\n\n\\[ x^2 = 729 \\]\n\nTo solve for \\( x \\), we need to take the square root of both sides of the equation. Since \\( x \\) is positive, we only take the positive square root:\n\n\\[ x = \\sqrt{729} \\]\n\nNext, we simplify \\( \\sqrt{729} \\). We know that \\( 729 \\) can be factored into prime factors:\n\n\\[ 729 = 27 \\times 27 = 3^3 \\times 3^3 = (3^3)^2 = 27^2 \\]\n\nThus, the square root of \\( 729 \\) is:\n\n\\[ \\sqrt{729} = \\sqrt{27^2} = 27 \\]\n\nSince \\( x \\) is positive, we have:\n\n\\[ x = 27 \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( x \\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{27}\n\\]",
